# tar --exclude-from patterns used by bin/deploy.sh when copying
# /home/smartqaq/repositories/hodlekki/  ->  /home/smartqaq/public_html/hodlc.lpc.cm/
#
# FORMAT: this file is read by GNU tar, not rsync. Two rules matter:
#
#   1. tar compares each pattern with the archive member name, which is
#      "./path/to/file" because bin/deploy.sh archives with `-C "$REPO" .`.
#      So a ROOT-ONLY entry is written "./name" (and "./assets/uploads"
#      for a nested one). Excluding a directory excludes everything in it.
#   2. tar SILENTLY IGNORES any pattern that starts or ends with "/"
#      (verified with GNU tar 1.35). "tests/" and "/AGENTS.md" match
#      nothing at all - that was open item O16.
#
# A BARE name with no slash matches that name at ANY depth, because tar's
# exclusion patterns are unanchored by default. Use that form only when
# the file should be skipped wherever it appears (".env", "error_log").
#
# tar never deletes. Anything excluded here is simply not copied, which is
# how runtime files (.env, root .htaccess, .user.ini, uploads/, error_log)
# survive in the docroot across deploys - the docroot copy is authoritative.

# Git internals & CI files (never belong in the docroot)
./.git
./.github
./.cpanel.yml
./.deployignore

# Environment / secrets (docroot copy is authoritative).
# Bare, so a stray .env in any subdirectory is skipped too.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# cPanel-generated PHP config at the root (docroot copy is authoritative).
# Root-anchored so nested config files like webhook/.htaccess still deploy.
./.htaccess
./.user.ini
./php.ini

# Runtime member/media uploads (docroot copy is authoritative)
./uploads
./assets/uploads

# PHP error logs (per-directory, generated at runtime). Bare: any depth.
error_log

# Vendored dependencies - regenerated by `composer install` in the deploy step
./vendor

# Local dev tooling & artefacts. The three root files are anchored because
# the module CSS build adds assets/se/css/input.css, which must deploy.
./composer.phar
./tailwindcss-linux-x64
./input.css
./tailwind.config.js
node_modules

# Repo-only docs (internal design and ops notes, never public).
# docs/.htaccess also denies web access as a fallback.
./DEPLOY.md
./AGENTS.md
./docs

# Developer test scripts - never serve these from the docroot
./tests

# IDE / OS junk (bare: any depth)
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
